 @TheCosmicMason  I recognise that a lot of people and especially console players have a poor understanding of graphics rendering hardware, but that doesn't also mean GPU companies and lazy/cheap game studios aren't screwing us over. 

If you compare actual optimised games that still look great like Doom Eternal, Death Stranding 2, RE4 Remake, etc. to the absolute garbage optimisation in games like Black Myth Wukong, Alan Wake 2, Monster Hunter Wilds, etc. it's a night and day difference. We could absolutely be getting games that run at higher resolutions and FPS while still looking cutting edge, but the studios would rather cut costs by not optimising the games and using overrated tech like RTX so they can put the burden on the consumer to pay for getting the game to run well. 

GPU companies and especially Nvidia have been getting more and more exploitative and anti-consumer in the last several years. The 50 series removed 32-bit PhysX and are the most cut down dies compared to the flagship (5090) to date while also being the most expensive, even at MSRP. Not to mention they still have pathetic amounts of VRAM as a form of planned obsolescence. Nvidia's profit margins are insane because their plan is to give us the bare minimum while increasing profit margins and design them so we need to buy a new card again in 3-4 years lest we start having to lower our settings or get sub-60 FPS. AMD is better, but still overpricing their GPUs and putting too little VRAM on their low-end cards.
